<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (In May 2026, the Mumbai Conclave of Religions brought faith leaders, scholars, artists and civil society members together to consider religious extremism and harmony with nature. Its key messages called for moving beyond symbolic coexistence toward everyday ethical responsibility, rejecting violence and hatred, and recognizing the links between ecological destruction and social injustice. Follow-up priorities included sustaining interfaith dialogue, promoting environmental stewardship, using art and education to nurture empathy, and turning belief into practical community action.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
