<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (It is in this spirit that the Inter-Religious Solidarity Council \(IRSC\) seeks to bring together religious leaders, faith communities and conscientious members of civil society. Our endeavour is founded on the conviction that meaningful dialogue can transform suspicion into understanding, indifference into friendship, and differences into opportunities for learning. Religious harmony does not require us to abandon our distinctive beliefs or traditions. Rather, it invites us to appreciate the values we share while respecting the convictions that make each tradition unique.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (From the perspective of Sanatan Dharma, the recognition of a deeper spiritual kinship among living beings provides a powerful foundation for harmony. The Bhagavad-gita \(5.18\) describes the wise as seeing with equal vision, recognising the spiritual worth of all beings beyond external distinctions. This vision encourages us to look beyond labels of religion, )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
