/T (Religious & Moral leaders like Gandhiji have always believed that Faith is strongest when freely chosen, as a voluntary submission to God rather than something imposed by birth or pressure and that the aim of humanity should be that every person becomes a better follower of the Faith they freely choose. It is for this very reason that IRSC has always held that conversion must spring from genuine personal conviction, never from inducement, deceit or mass campaigns. This Act appears to be at odds with these principles.)
