/E (The discussions highlighted the need for critical examination within religious communities. Traditions that offer profound teachings on compassion, justice and non-violence must also confront practices and interpretations that perpetuate caste hierarchies, patriarchy, exclusion and hostility towards dissent. Anti-caste perspectives are essential to any meaningful engagement with religion and social justice. The use of religion to legitimise discrimination, hostility or violence against LGBTQIA+ people, including mobilisation against their equal rights and relationships, demands particular scrutiny. Religious freedom carries with it the responsibility to respect the dignity and freedoms of others.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
